---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Chart from '../components/Chart.astro';
import { asset } from '../lib/paths';
import { monitored, verified, manualCost, ourCost } from '../data/series';
---

<Base>
  <main>
    <section class="hero" id="platform">
      <div class="col">
        <span class="logo" role="img" aria-label="Carbon Valinor" style={`--logo: url(${asset('logo.svg')})`}></span>
        <p data-words>
          <span class="lead" role="heading" aria-level="1">Carbon Valinor builds software for carbon.</span>{' '}
          We build the operating system for carbon management: the software a company
          uses to run its CO₂ chain end to end, from capture plant and compression to
          pipeline, injection well and reservoir. It connects to the machines and
          sensors in the field, runs physical and machine-learning models on what they
          measure, and controls, forecasts and records each stage as one system.
        </p>
        <p data-words>
          We want permanent storage to be cheap to run and cheap to prove. Once it is,
          storing carbon stops being a last resort and becomes the default.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="col" id="monitoring">
      <p data-words>
        <span class="lead">Every tonne, accounted for.</span>{' '}
        Our models work on wellhead and downhole pressure, distributed fibre-optic
        sensing, time-lapse seismic, satellite radar of surface deformation and
        soil-gas flux. Reservoir simulations are matched to field history as the data
        arrives, and anomaly-detection models learn how each site normally behaves.
        Together they track <span class="counter" data-keep>1,243,118</span> tonnes so
        far. When pressure drifts, a plume leaves its predicted footprint or two meters
        disagree, the system localises the cause and alerts the operator. Mass is
        reconciled from capture to injection, and every reading is kept with a
        timestamp, in formats regulators and registries accept.
      </p>
      <Chart
        id="stored"
        series={[
          { label: 'CO₂ monitored', value: '1.24 Mt', data: monitored },
          { label: 'Verified', value: '1.17 Mt', data: verified },
        ]}
      />
    </section>

    <section class="col" id="cost">
      <p data-words>
        <span class="lead">Cheaper every year.</span>{' '}
        Monitoring, reporting and verification add real cost to every stored tonne,
        and most of it is still manual work. We automate the measurement, the
        modelling and the reconciliation, so the cost per tonne falls each year and
        the evidence holds to the same standard.
      </p>
      <Chart
        id="cost"
        series={[
          { label: 'Manual, per tonne', value: '$18.40', data: manualCost },
          { label: 'With Carbon Valinor', value: '$4.20', data: ourCost },
        ]}
      />
    </section>

    <section class="col" id="contact">
      <p data-words>
        <span class="lead">Work with us.</span>{' '}
        We work with operators across the CO₂ chain: capture, transport, storage and
        accounting. If you run any part of it, write to us.
      </p>
      <p class="closing" data-words>
        <a class="mail" href="mailto:info@carbonvalinor.com">info@carbonvalinor.com</a>
      </p>
      <footer><span data-words>© 2026 Carbon Valinor</span></footer>
    </section>
  </main>
</Base>
